<title>SPAIN: BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP DRAW.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP DRAW.</headline>
<dateline>BARCELONA 1997-03-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The draw for the 1997 men's</p>
<p>European basketball championship, to be played in Spain from</p>
<p>June 25-July 6, was made on Saturday as follows:</p>
<p>Group A (in  Gerona)</p>
<p>Greece,  Bosnia Herzegovina, Russia, Turkey</p>
<p>Group B  (Gerona)</p>
<p>Lithuania, Slovenia, France, Israel</p>
<p>Group C (Badalona)</p>
<p>Yugoslavia, Latvia, Italy, Poland</p>
<p>Group D (Badalona)</p>
<p>Croatia, Ukraine, Spain, Germany</p>
<p>Note: Groups play on a round-robin basis with the top three</p>
<p>teams qualifying for the following stage which will be played in</p>
<p>two groups of six.</p>
<p>The four best placed teams then qualify for the</p>
<p>quarter-finals played on a knock-out basis.</p>
</text>
